# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Background {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Every IBM Quantum&reg; QPU reports a set of properties that describe the current performance of its qubits: relaxation times ($T_1$), coherence times ($T_2$), readout errors, and one- and two-qubit gate errors. These numbers matter in practice. The transpiler uses them to select the physical qubits for your circuit, error mitigation techniques rely on them, and you might use them to judge whether a device is working well enough for an experiment.\n"
msgstr "Ang bawat IBM Quantum&reg; QPU ay nag-uulat ng isang set ng mga property na naglalarawan sa kasalukuyang performance ng mga qubit nito: relaxation times ($T_1$), coherence times ($T_2$), readout errors, at one- at two-qubit gate errors. Ang mga numerong ito ay mahalaga sa praktika. Ginagamit ito ng transpiler upang piliin ang mga physical qubit para sa iyong circuit, umaasa dito ang mga error mitigation technique, at maaari mo itong gamitin upang husgahan kung sapat na kaayos ang isang device para sa isang eksperimento.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The reported properties come from calibration procedures that typically run about once a day. Superconducting qubits, however, can drift on shorter timescales, and transient defects (known as two-level systems) can temporarily degrade a qubit that performed well at calibration time. In addition, you often transpile a job well before it runs, so decisions based on the reported properties can depend on outdated information.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga iniulat na property ay nagmumula sa mga calibration procedure na karaniwang tumatakbo minsan sa isang araw. Ang mga superconducting qubit, gayunpaman, ay maaaring mag-drift sa mas maiikling timescale, at ang mga transient defect (kilala bilang two-level systems) ay maaaring pansamantalang magpababa ng kalidad ng isang qubit na maganda ang performance noong panahon ng calibration. Bukod dito, madalas mong i-transpile ang isang job nang matagal bago ito tumakbo, kaya ang mga desisyong nakabatay sa mga iniulat na property ay maaaring nakasalalay sa lumang impormasyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses the `BackendCharacterization` utility from [Qiskit Device Benchmarking](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-device-benchmarking), which combines experiment construction, job submission, and curve fitting into a few calls. For roughly 70 seconds of QPU time, you receive a backend object whose properties reflect the current state of the device. You can compare these properties against the reported values or pass the backend to other tools. The final example uses the refreshed values to select physical qubits for a GHZ-state circuit and compares the results with those of the same circuit compiled with the reported properties.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng tutorial na ito ang `BackendCharacterization` utility mula sa [Qiskit Device Benchmarking](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-device-benchmarking), na pinagsasama ang pagbuo ng eksperimento, pagsusumite ng job, at curve fitting sa ilang tawag lamang. Sa humigit-kumulang 70 segundo ng oras ng QPU, makakatanggap ka ng backend object na ang mga property ay sumasalamin sa kasalukuyang estado ng device. Maaari mong ihambing ang mga property na ito sa mga iniulat na halaga o ipasa ang backend sa ibang mga tool. Ginagamit ng huling halimbawa ang mga na-refresh na halaga para pumili ng mga physical qubit para sa isang GHZ-state circuit at inihahambing ang mga resulta sa resulta ng parehong circuit na na-compile gamit ang mga iniulat na property.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The characterization experiments {#the-characterization-experiments}"
msgstr "Ang mga characterization experiment {#the-characterization-experiments}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The suite measures five properties, each with a standard experiment:\n"
msgstr "Sinusukat ng suite ang limang property, bawat isa ay may standard na eksperimento:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Readout error** (`readout`): The experiment prepares each qubit in $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$ and immediately measures it. The probability of a wrong readout gives the state preparation and measurement (SPAM) error.\n"
msgstr "**Readout error** (`readout`): Inihahanda ng eksperimento ang bawat qubit sa $|0\\rangle$ o $|1\\rangle$ at agad itong sinusukat. Ang probability ng maling readout ay nagbibigay ng state preparation and measurement (SPAM) error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Single-qubit gate error** (`rb_1q`): Randomized benchmarking (RB) runs sequences of random single-qubit Clifford gates that ideally compose to the identity. The decay of the survival probability with sequence length gives the average error per gate, independent of SPAM errors.\n"
msgstr "**Single-qubit gate error** (`rb_1q`): Ang Randomized benchmarking (RB) ay nagpapatakbo ng mga sequence ng random na single-qubit Clifford gate na sa ideal ay bumubuo sa identity. Ang pagbaba ng survival probability habang tumataas ang haba ng sequence ay nagbibigay ng average error kada gate, independiyente sa mga SPAM error.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two-qubit gate error** (`rb_2q`): This experiment applies the same RB method to full layers of non-overlapping two-qubit gates that run simultaneously, as in a [layer fidelity](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.05933) experiment. Because many gates run at once, the resulting error rates include crosstalk effects and are closer to the error rates in a deep circuit.\n"
msgstr "**Two-qubit gate error** (`rb_2q`): Inilalapat ng eksperimentong ito ang parehong RB method sa buong layer ng non-overlapping two-qubit gate na sabay-sabay na tumatakbo, tulad ng sa isang eksperimentong [layer fidelity](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.05933). Dahil maraming gate ang tumatakbo nang sabay-sabay, kasama sa resultang error rate ang mga epekto ng crosstalk at mas malapit ito sa mga error rate sa isang malalim na circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_1$** (`t1`): The experiment excites each qubit and measures it after increasing delays. The decay of the excited-state population gives the relaxation time.\n"
msgstr "**$T_1$** (`t1`): Ine-excite ng eksperimento ang bawat qubit at sinusukat ito pagkatapos ng lumalaking delay. Ang pagbaba ng excited-state population ay nagbibigay ng relaxation time.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_2$** (`t2`): A Hahn echo experiment puts each qubit in a superposition, applies an echo pulse halfway through a delay, and measures how quickly the qubit loses phase coherence. By default, the experiment uses a single echo. A later section of this tutorial demonstrates a multi-echo (CPMG-style) variant.\n"
msgstr "**$T_2$** (`t2`): Inilalagay ng isang Hahn echo experiment ang bawat qubit sa superposition, naglalapat ng echo pulse sa kalagitnaan ng isang delay, at sinusukat kung gaano kabilis nawawala ng qubit ang phase coherence. Bilang default, iisang echo ang ginagamit ng eksperimento. Ipinapakita ng isang susunod na seksyon ng tutorial na ito ang isang multi-echo (CPMG-style) na variant.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scope and limits of the refreshed properties {#scope-and-limits-of-the-refreshed-properties}"
msgstr "Saklaw at mga limitasyon ng mga na-refresh na property {#scope-and-limits-of-the-refreshed-properties}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the following points in mind when you use this workflow:\n"
msgstr "Isaisip ang mga sumusunod na punto kapag ginagamit mo ang workflow na ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The refreshed properties exist only in the backend object that the utility returns to you. Nothing changes on the device itself or in the calibration data that IBM Quantum reports to other users.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga na-refresh na property ay umiiral lamang sa backend object na ibinabalik ng utility sa iyo. Walang nagbabago sa mismong device o sa calibration data na iniuulat ng IBM Quantum sa ibang gumagamit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The measured values are a snapshot taken with a particular methodology. Some of them, notably the layered two-qubit errors and the parallel single-echo $T_2$ values, are measured differently from the reported calibration data, so part of any gap that you observe comes from methodology rather than drift. This tutorial identifies these cases.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga sinukat na halaga ay isang snapshot na kinuha gamit ang isang partikular na methodology. Ang ilan sa mga ito, lalo na ang layered two-qubit errors at ang parallel single-echo $T_2$ na halaga, ay sinusukat nang iba mula sa iniulat na calibration data, kaya bahagi ng anumang pagkakaiba na iyong maoobserbahan ay galing sa methodology sa halip na drift. Tinutukoy ng tutorial na ito ang mga kasong ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The characterization itself costs QPU time (about 70 seconds for the full suite on a 156-qubit Heron processor), which is the cost of current information.\n"
msgstr "Ang characterization mismo ay gumagamit ng oras ng QPU (humigit-kumulang 70 segundo para sa buong suite sa isang 156-qubit na Heron processor), na siyang gastos ng kasalukuyang impormasyon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The workflow follows the four steps of a Qiskit pattern:\n"
msgstr "Sinusunod ng workflow ang apat na hakbang ng isang Qiskit pattern:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem.** Choose the device and the set of properties to measure.\n"
msgstr "**Hakbang 1: I-map ang mga classical input sa isang quantum na problema.** Piliin ang device at ang set ng mga property na susukatin.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution.** The utility builds the experiment circuits directly in the native gates of the device and parallelizes them across the device.\n"
msgstr "**Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pagpapatakbo sa quantum hardware.** Direktang binubuo ng utility ang mga experiment circuit sa native gates ng device at pinararalel ang mga ito sa buong device.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives.** The experiments run as Sampler jobs inside a batch.\n"
msgstr "**Hakbang 3: Mag-execute gamit ang Qiskit primitives.** Tumatakbo ang mga eksperimento bilang Sampler job sa loob ng isang batch.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format.** Fit the measurement data into per-qubit error maps, refresh the backend, and compare the measured properties against the reported ones.\n"
msgstr "**Hakbang 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical format.** I-fit ang measurement data sa mga per-qubit error map, i-refresh ang backend, at ihambing ang mga sinukat na property laban sa mga iniulat.\n"

