# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa ng simulator sa maliit na sukat {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial does not include a simulator example. The workflow measures the physical imperfections of a specific device: how quickly its qubits relax and dephase, and how often its gates and readout fail. An ideal simulator has none of these imperfections, so there is nothing to characterize. If you attach a synthetic noise model to a fake backend, the experiments only recover the values that you put in the model. For that reason, this tutorial proceeds directly to hardware, in the four steps of a Qiskit pattern.\n"
msgstr "Hindi kasama sa tutorial na ito ang isang simulator example. Sinusukat ng workflow ang mga physical imperfection ng isang tiyak na device: kung gaano kabilis nag-relax at nag-dephase ang mga qubit nito, at kung gaano kadalas nabibigo ang mga gate at readout nito. Walang alinman sa mga imperfection na ito ang isang ideal na simulator, kaya walang dapat i-characterize. Kung maglalagay ka ng synthetic noise model sa isang fake backend, ang mga eksperimento ay magbabalik lamang ng mga halagang inilagay mo sa model. Dahil dito, direktang magpapatuloy ang tutorial na ito sa hardware, sa apat na hakbang ng isang Qiskit pattern.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Large-scale hardware example {#large-scale-hardware-example}"
msgstr "Halimbawa sa malaking sukat na hardware {#large-scale-hardware-example}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-09 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1: I-map ang mga classical input sa isang quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this workflow, the \"problem\" is the device itself. The classical inputs are the QPU that you want to characterize and the list of properties to measure. The quantum experiments are the characterization circuits that the utility generates from these inputs.\n"
msgstr "Sa workflow na ito, ang \"problema\" ay ang device mismo. Ang classical inputs ay ang QPU na nais mong i-characterize at ang listahan ng mga property na susukatin. Ang quantum experiments ay ang mga characterization circuit na binubuo ng utility mula sa mga input na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, select the least-busy available QPU with a minimum of 120 qubits. The results in this tutorial were collected on `ibm_boston`, a Heron r3 processor, on 6 October 2026.\n"
msgstr "Una, piliin ang pinakamaluwag na available na QPU na may hindi bababa sa 120 qubit. Ang mga resulta sa tutorial na ito ay nakolekta sa `ibm_boston`, isang Heron r3 processor, noong 6 Oktubre 2026.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, choose which properties to measure. You can pass any subset of the following experiments:\n"
msgstr "Susunod, piliin kung aling mga properties ang susukatin. Maaari kang magpasa ng anumang subset ng mga sumusunod na eksperimento:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`readout`: SPAM (state preparation and measurement) experiment\n"
msgstr "`readout`: SPAM (state preparation and measurement) na eksperimento\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`rb_1q`: isolated single-qubit randomized benchmarking\n"
msgstr "`rb_1q`: nakahiwalay na single-qubit randomized benchmarking\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`rb_2q`: simultaneous two-qubit randomized benchmarking from a layer fidelity experiment\n"
msgstr "`rb_2q`: sabayang two-qubit randomized benchmarking mula sa layer fidelity na eksperimento\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`t2`: $T_2$ Hahn echo experiment (a single echo by default)\n"
msgstr "`t2`: $T_2$ Hahn echo na eksperimento (iisang echo bilang default)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`t1`: $T_1$ relaxation experiment\n"
msgstr "`t1`: $T_1$ relaxation na eksperimento\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the full suite to characterize the device completely. To save QPU time, remove the entries for any properties that you do not need.\n"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang buong suite para ganap na ma-characterize ang device. Para makatipid ng oras ng QPU, alisin ang mga entry ng anumang property na hindi mo kailangan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pagsasagawa gamit ang quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In most tutorials, this step is where you transpile your circuits. In this tutorial, `BackendCharacterization` handles transpilation internally. It builds the experiment circuits directly in the native gates of the device, runs the single-qubit experiments on all qubits in parallel, and schedules the two-qubit benchmarking over disjoint layers of the coupling map, so that a small number of jobs cover the entire device. Because of this parallelization, the whole suite uses only about 70 seconds of QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Sa karamihan ng mga tutorial, dito mo ita-transpile ang iyong mga circuit. Sa tutorial na ito, ang `BackendCharacterization` ang humahawak ng transpilation sa loob. Binubuo nito ang mga experiment circuit nang direkta sa native gates ng device, pinapatakbo ang single-qubit experiments sa lahat ng qubit nang sabay-sabay, at itinatakda ang two-qubit benchmarking sa magkakahiwalay na layer ng coupling map, kaya ilang job lang ang sumasaklaw sa buong device. Dahil sa parallelization na ito, humigit-kumulang 70 segundo lang ng oras ng QPU ang ginagamit ng buong suite.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialize the class that manages the workflow:\n"
msgstr "I-initialize ang class na namamahala sa workflow:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3: Isagawa gamit ang Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `run_experiments` method builds the circuits and submits them as [Sampler](/guides/get-started-with-sampler) jobs. Run it inside a [`Batch`](/guides/run-jobs-batch) context so that the jobs are scheduled together on the QPU. The method returns after it submits all of the jobs. You can also run the method outside a `Batch` or inside a `Session`.\n"
msgstr "Ang `run_experiments` method ay bumubuo ng mga circuit at isinusumite ang mga ito bilang mga [Sampler](/guides/get-started-with-sampler) job. Patakbuhin ito sa loob ng [`Batch`](/guides/run-jobs-batch) context para maka-schedule ang mga job nang magkakasama sa QPU. Nagbabalik ang method pagkatapos nitong isumite ang lahat ng job. Maaari mo ring patakbuhin ang method sa labas ng `Batch` o sa loob ng `Session`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"You might see a warning that a backend was passed while a session context manager is open. This warning is expected, and you can safely ignore it. The layer fidelity experiment might also warn that it does not use the optional `xslow` gate. You can ignore this warning too, because the experiment uses supported standard single-qubit gates.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Maaaring makakita ka ng babala na may ipinasang backend habang bukas ang isang session context manager. Inaasahan ang babalang ito, at ligtas mo itong balewalain. Maaari ring magbabala ang layer fidelity experiment na hindi nito ginagamit ang opsyonal na `xslow` gate. Maaari mo rin itong balewalain, dahil gumagamit ang eksperimento ng mga sinusuportahang karaniwang single-qubit gate.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The method returns the submitted jobs as a dictionary with one entry per experiment. Use this dictionary to track the jobs on the [IBM Quantum Platform dashboard](/guides/monitor-job) or to debug them.\n"
msgstr "Ibinabalik ng method ang mga naisumiteng job bilang dictionary na may isang entry bawat eksperimento. Gamitin ang dictionary na ito para subaybayan ang mga job sa [IBM Quantum Platform dashboard](/guides/monitor-job) o para i-debug ang mga ito.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Step 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze the results {#analyze-the-results}"
msgstr "Suriin ang mga resulta {#analyze-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `analyze_results` method waits for the jobs to finish and then processes the measurement data. It fits exponential decays to the $T_1$ and $T_2$ data, fits survival-probability decays to the RB data, and computes assignment matrices for readout. It returns a dictionary of *error maps*, with one entry per measured property. Each error map assigns a measured value to each qubit (or qubit pair).\n"
msgstr "Naghihintay ang `analyze_results` method na matapos ang mga job at pagkatapos ay pino-proseso ang measurement data. Ini-fit nito ang exponential decay sa $T_1$ at $T_2$ data, ini-fit ang survival-probability decay sa RB data, at kinukuwenta ang assignment matrices para sa readout. Nagbabalik ito ng dictionary ng *error maps*, na may isang entry bawat sinukat na property. Nagtatalaga ang bawat error map ng sinukat na halaga sa bawat qubit (o pares ng qubit).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maps cover readout error, the single-qubit `x` and `sx` gate errors, the layered two-qubit errors (`lf_error_map`, from the layer fidelity experiment), and the $T_1$ and $T_2$ times in seconds.\n"
msgstr "Sinasaklaw ng mga map ang readout error, ang single-qubit `x` at `sx` gate errors, ang layered two-qubit errors (`lf_error_map`, mula sa layer fidelity na eksperimento), at ang mga oras ng $T_1$ at $T_2$ sa segundo.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the backend properties {#update-the-backend-properties}"
msgstr "I-update ang mga backend property {#update-the-backend-properties}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `update_backend` method writes the measured values into the properties of a copy of the backend and returns the copy. The original `backend` object keeps the reported calibration data, so that you can compare the two sets of properties, as shown in the next section. This update applies only to your Python session. It does not change anything on the device or for other users.\n"
msgstr "Isinusulat ng `update_backend` method ang mga sinukat na halaga sa mga property ng kopya ng backend at ibinabalik ang kopya. Pinapanatili ng orihinal na `backend` object ang iniulat na calibration data, para maihambing mo ang dalawang set ng property, gaya ng ipinapakita sa susunod na seksyon. Sa iyong Python session lang naaapektuhan ng update na ito. Hindi ito nagbabago ng anuman sa device o para sa ibang user.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the measured properties against the reported ones {#compare-the-measured-properties-against-the-reported-ones}"
msgstr "Ikumpara ang mga sinukat na property sa mga naiulat na property {#compare-the-measured-properties-against-the-reported-ones}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, plot the measured real-time properties against the values that the backend reports. In each panel, the qubits (or qubit pairs) are sorted by measured value, so the measured curve is smooth by construction. The scatter of the reported values around this curve shows where the two data sets disagree. The single-qubit RB results appear in one plot, because the utility assigns the same measured error per gate to both the `x` and `sx` gates. The axis limits are based on most of the data, so that a few extreme outliers do not compress the plots. An annotation on each plot counts any points that fall outside the range. To set the limits yourself, pass the `ylim` argument.\n"
msgstr "Sa wakas, i-plot ang mga sinukat na real-time property laban sa mga halagang iniuulat ng backend. Sa bawat panel, ang mga qubit (o pares ng qubit) ay pinagsunod-sunod ayon sa sinukat na halaga, kaya smooth ang measured curve dahil sa pagkakabuo nito. Ang scatter ng mga iniulat na halaga sa paligid ng curve na ito ay nagpapakita kung saan hindi nagtutugma ang dalawang data set. Lumilitaw sa isang plot ang mga resulta ng single-qubit RB, dahil itinatalaga ng utility ang parehong sinukat na error bawat gate sa parehong `x` at `sx` gate. Nakabatay ang mga axis limit sa karamihan ng data, para hindi ma-compress ang mga plot ng ilang matinding outlier. Binibilang ng isang annotation sa bawat plot ang anumang punto na nasa labas ng range. Para itakda mo mismo ang mga limit, ipasa ang `ylim` argument.\n"

