# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read these plots carefully, because not every gap between the two curves means that the device has drifted:\n"
msgstr "Basahin nang maingat ang mga plot na ito, dahil hindi lahat ng puwang sa pagitan ng dalawang curve ay nangangahulugang nag-drift ang device:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Readout and single-qubit errors**: The measured values track the reported ones for most qubits, but for a few qubits the reported value is far from the measured curve. These localized disagreements can reflect the drift that this workflow is designed to detect.\n"
msgstr "**Readout at single-qubit errors**: Sinusundan ng mga sinukat na halaga ang mga iniulat sa karamihan ng mga qubit, pero para sa ilang qubit, malayo ang iniulat na halaga sa measured curve. Maaaring sumasalamin ang mga naka-localize na hindi pagtutugmang ito sa drift na idinisenyo ng workflow na ito na matukoy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_1$**: The two data sets scatter around each other with no systematic offset, which is consistent with natural fluctuation of $T_1$ over time.\n"
msgstr "**$T_1$**: Ang dalawang set ng data ay nag-scatter sa paligid ng isa't isa nang walang systematic offset, na naaayon sa natural na pagbabago-bago ng $T_1$ sa paglipas ng panahon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Two-qubit errors**: The measured values are systematically above the reported ones. This difference is expected, because the reported values come from isolated gates, while the layer fidelity experiment runs many gates simultaneously and therefore includes crosstalk. The layered values are more relevant for deep circuits, but they are not directly comparable to the reported calibration data.\n"
msgstr "**Two-qubit errors**: Ang mga sinukat na halaga ay sistematikong *mas mataas* kaysa sa mga naiulat. Inaasahan ito, dahil ang mga naiulat na halaga ay galing sa nakahiwalay na gates, habang pinapatakbo ng layer fidelity na eksperimento ang maraming gates nang sabay-sabay kaya kasama na ang crosstalk. Mas relevant ang layered na mga halaga para sa malalalim na circuit, ngunit hindi ito direktang maikukumpara sa naiulat na calibration data.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**$T_2$**: The measured values are well below the reported ones for most qubits. As with the two-qubit errors, methodology plays a large role, which the next section examines.\n"
msgstr "**$T_2$**: Mas mababa nang malaki ang mga sinukat na halaga kaysa sa mga iniulat para sa karamihan ng qubit. Tulad ng sa two-qubit errors, malaki ang papel ng methodology, na sinusuri ng susunod na seksyon.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect individual experiment results {#inspect-individual-experiment-results}"
msgstr "Suriin ang mga indibidwal na resulta ng eksperimento {#inspect-individual-experiment-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can also inspect the raw results of the individual characterization experiments through the `experiment_data` property, which returns the underlying [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/) `ExperimentData` objects. For example, the following code displays the measured $T_1$ decay curve of a single qubit. Use a curve like this one to check the quality of a fit before you rely on the value that the fit produced.\n"
msgstr "Maaari mo ring suriin ang raw na resulta ng mga indibidwal na characterization experiment sa pamamagitan ng `experiment_data` property, na nagbabalik ng mga underlying [Qiskit Experiments](https://qiskit-community.github.io/qiskit-experiments/) `ExperimentData` objects. Halimbawa, ipinapakita ng sumusunod na code ang sinukat na $T_1$ decay curve ng isang qubit. Gamitin ang ganitong curve upang suriin ang kalidad ng fit bago mo paniwalaan ang value na nabuo nito.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-28-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-28-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measure T2 with a dynamical decoupling train {#measure-t2-with-a-dynamical-decoupling-train}"
msgstr "Sukatin ang T2 gamit ang dynamical decoupling train {#measure-t2-with-a-dynamical-decoupling-train}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default, the $T_2$ experiment applies a single Hahn echo and measures all qubits in parallel. As the previous comparison plot shows, this method can produce noticeably lower $T_2$ values than the backend reports. One possible cause is the number of echoes. The reported values might come from a calibration that uses dynamical decoupling, which suppresses low-frequency noise. To test this hypothesis, run a $T_2$-only characterization with a larger value of `t2_num_echoes`, which applies a CPMG-style train of echo pulses. In both cases, the delays represent the total free-evolution time, so the fitted $T_2$ values are directly comparable to the single-echo results.\n"
msgstr "Bilang default, naglalapat ang $T_2$ na eksperimento ng iisang Hahn echo at sinusukat ang lahat ng qubit nang sabay-sabay. Gaya ng ipinapakita ng nakaraang comparison plot, maaaring magbunga ang paraang ito ng kapansin-pansing mas mababang $T_2$ na halaga kaysa sa iniuulat ng backend. Isang posibleng dahilan ang bilang ng echoes. Maaaring nagmula ang mga iniulat na halaga sa isang calibration na gumagamit ng dynamical decoupling, na pumipigil sa low-frequency noise. Para masubukan ang hypothesis na ito, magpatakbo ng $T_2$-only na characterization na may mas malaking halaga ng `t2_num_echoes`, na naglalapat ng CPMG-style na train ng echo pulses. Sa parehong kaso, kumakatawan ang mga delay sa kabuuang free-evolution time, kaya direktang maikukumpara ang mga fitted na halaga ng $T_2$ sa mga resulta ng single-echo.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-31-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/cell-31-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this run, the extra echoes barely changed the result. The 8-echo median (77 &micro;s) is close to the single-echo median (75 &micro;s), and both remain far below the reported median (300 &micro;s). The number of echoes alone does not explain this gap. Other methodological differences also contribute, such as details of the calibration procedure, and measurement of all qubits in parallel instead of in isolation.\n"
msgstr "Sa run na ito, halos hindi nagbago ang resulta dahil sa dagdag na echoes. Ang 8-echo median (77 &micro;s) ay malapit sa single-echo median (75 &micro;s), at pareho pa ring lubhang mas mababa sa naiulat na median (300 &micro;s). Ang bilang lang ng echoes ay hindi sapat para ipaliwanag ang gap na ito. May iba pang methodological na pagkakaiba na nag-aambag din, tulad ng mga detalye ng calibration procedure, at pagsukat sa lahat ng qubit nang sabay-sabay sa halip na nakahiwalay.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Therefore, compare $T_2$ values (and layered two-qubit errors) across methodologies with care. The refreshed values are a self-consistent snapshot, taken under conditions close to those of a real workload. These values are well suited to compare qubits with each other or to track a device over time. A gap relative to the reported calibration data, however, is not automatically evidence of drift.\n"
msgstr "Kaya, ihambing nang maingat ang mga halaga ng $T_2$ (at layered two-qubit errors) sa iba't ibang methodology. Ang mga na-refresh na halaga ay isang self-consistent na snapshot, na kinuha sa ilalim ng mga kondisyong malapit sa aktwal na workload. Angkop ang mga halagang ito para ihambing ang mga qubit sa isa't isa o para subaybayan ang isang device sa paglipas ng panahon. Ang isang gap kaugnay ng naiulat na calibration data, gayunpaman, ay hindi awtomatikong ebidensya ng drift.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run steps 1–4 in a single call {#run-steps-14-in-a-single-call}"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang mga hakbang 1–4 sa iisang tawag {#run-steps-14-in-a-single-call}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For routine use, you rarely need the intermediate results. The `run_and_update` method combines the previous steps (build, submit, fit, and update) into a single call that returns the refreshed backend. It accepts the same `experiments` list and forwards options such as `t2_num_echoes`. You can also wrap it in a `Batch` or `Session` context.\n"
msgstr "Para sa karaniwang paggamit, bihira mong kailanganin ang mga intermediate na resulta. Pinagsasama ng `run_and_update` method ang mga naunang hakbang (build, submit, fit, at update) sa iisang tawag na nagbabalik ng na-refresh na backend. Tinatanggap nito ang parehong `experiments` list at ipinapasa ang mga opsyon tulad ng `t2_num_echoes`. Maaari mo rin itong i-wrap sa isang `Batch` o `Session` context.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The following cell does not return until all jobs and post-processing are complete.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Hindi magbabalik ang sumusunod na cell hanggang matapos ang lahat ng job at post-processing.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The refreshed `backend_updated` object is ready for the GHZ comparison in the next section. Refresh the properties close to execution time to reduce the effect of further device drift.\n"
msgstr "Handa na ang na-refresh na `backend_updated` object para sa paghahambing ng GHZ sa susunod na seksyon. I-refresh ang mga property malapit sa oras ng execution para mabawasan ang epekto ng karagdagang device drift.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use refreshed properties for qubit selection {#use-refreshed-properties-for-qubit-selection}"
msgstr "Gamitin ang mga na-refresh na property para sa pagpili ng qubit {#use-refreshed-properties-for-qubit-selection}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This optional example completes the workflow. It checks whether the refreshed properties lead to better circuit results. It compiles the same circuits twice, once with the reported properties and once with the refreshed properties. Then it runs both versions and compares their outputs. This example uses the `backend` and `backend_updated` objects from the previous sections, and it submits additional work to the QPU.\n"
msgstr "Kinukumpleto ng opsyonal na halimbawang ito ang workflow. Sinusuri nito kung ang mga na-refresh na property ay humahantong sa mas magagandang resulta ng circuit. Kino-compile nito ang parehong mga circuit nang dalawang beses, minsan gamit ang naiulat na mga property at minsan gamit ang na-refresh na mga property. Pagkatapos, pinapatakbo nito ang dalawang bersyon at inihahambing ang kanilang mga output. Ginagamit ng halimbawang ito ang mga `backend` at `backend_updated` object mula sa mga nakaraang seksyon, at nagsusumite ito ng karagdagang trabaho sa QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the comparison circuits {#build-the-comparison-circuits}"
msgstr "Buuin ang mga comparison circuit {#build-the-comparison-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare an $n$-qubit Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger (GHZ) state with a Hadamard gate followed by a chain of CNOT gates, and measure every qubit. Ideally, the outcomes $|0\\cdots0\\rangle$ and $|1\\cdots1\\rangle$ each have probability 0.5. Because you measure every qubit, an error on any qubit in the chain, including a readout error, reduces the probability of the ideal outcomes. The measured outputs are therefore sensitive to the physical qubits that the transpiler selects.\n"
msgstr "Maghanda ng $n$-qubit na Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger (GHZ) state gamit ang isang Hadamard gate na sinusundan ng chain ng mga CNOT gate, at sukatin ang bawat qubit. Sa ideyal, ang mga outcome na $|0\\cdots0\\rangle$ at $|1\\cdots1\\rangle$ ay may probabilidad na 0.5 bawat isa. Dahil sinusukat mo ang bawat qubit, binabawasan ng error sa alinmang qubit sa chain, kasama ang readout error, ang probabilidad ng mga ideal na outcome. Kaya, ang mga nasukat na output ay sensitibo sa mga pisikal na qubit na pinipili ng transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refreshed properties tend to matter most at moderate sizes, where the transpiler can choose from many candidate qubit chains. Very large circuits use most of the device, so the transpiler has little room to avoid poorly performing qubits. To save QPU time, reduce the list of circuit sizes.\n"
msgstr "Kadalasang pinakamahalaga ang mga na-refresh na property sa katamtamang laki, kung saan makakapili ang transpiler mula sa maraming kandidatong qubit chain. Ang napakalalaking circuit ay gumagamit ng karamihan ng device, kaya kaunti lang ang puwang ng transpiler para iwasan ang mga qubit na mahina ang performance. Para makatipid sa oras ng QPU, paliitin ang listahan ng mga laki ng circuit.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/selection-circuits-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/selection-circuits-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transpile with reported and refreshed properties {#transpile-with-reported-and-refreshed-properties}"
msgstr "Mag-transpile gamit ang naiulat at na-refresh na mga property {#transpile-with-reported-and-refreshed-properties}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The transpiler uses a `Target` to choose physical qubits and native instructions. If you update only the backend properties, an existing target can remain unchanged. Instead, copy the original target and explicitly apply the refreshed errors and coherence times to the copy. The copy keeps the original instruction durations and connectivity. If a coherence time is unavailable for a qubit, keep its existing target value.\n"
msgstr "Gumagamit ang transpiler ng `Target` para pumili ng mga pisikal na qubit at native na instruction. Kung ang mga backend property lang ang ia-update mo, maaaring manatiling hindi nagbabago ang umiiral na target. Sa halip, kopyahin ang orihinal na target at tahasang ilapat ang mga na-refresh na error at coherence time sa kopya. Pinananatili ng kopya ang orihinal na instruction duration at connectivity. Kung walang available na coherence time para sa isang qubit, panatilihin ang umiiral nitong halaga sa target.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A reported error of 1 means that the error is undefined, because benchmarking of that qubit or gate has not succeeded for several days, and the value is outdated (see [QPU information](/guides/qpu-information)). This value does not necessarily mean that the gate is not working, but you should treat the gate with caution. A single characterization run can still fit a low error for such a gate, so that the gate appears to be one of the best on the device. To be cautious, keep those entries at their reported value so that the transpiler continues to avoid them.\n"
msgstr "Ang naiulat na error na 1 ay nangangahulugang hindi tinukoy ang error, dahil hindi naging matagumpay ang benchmarking ng qubit o gate na iyon sa loob ng ilang araw, at luma na ang halaga (tingnan ang [QPU information](/guides/qpu-information)). Hindi ibig sabihin ng halagang ito na hindi gumagana ang gate, ngunit dapat mong ituring nang may pag-iingat ang gate. Ang isang characterization run ay maaari pa ring mag-fit ng mababang error para sa gayong gate, kaya lumilitaw na isa ito sa pinakamahusay sa device. Para mag-ingat, panatilihin ang mga entry na iyon sa naiulat na halaga nila para patuloy silang iwasan ng transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the same optimization level and random seed for both compilations so that the comparison controls for transpiler randomness.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang parehong optimization level at random seed para sa parehong compilation para makontrol ng paghahambing ang randomness ng transpiler.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you run the circuits, check how many physical qubits each refreshed layout changes. If the two compilations select the same qubits, the refreshed properties cannot make a difference for that circuit.\n"
msgstr "Bago mo patakbuhin ang mga circuit, tingnan kung ilang pisikal na qubit ang binabago ng bawat na-refresh na layout. Kung pareho ang mga qubit na pinili ng dalawang compilation, hindi makakagawa ng pagkakaiba ang mga na-refresh na property para sa circuit na iyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute both sets of circuits {#execute-both-sets-of-circuits}"
msgstr "Isagawa ang parehong set ng mga circuit {#execute-both-sets-of-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run both versions on the same QPU, with the same shot count and error suppression settings. Interleave the reported and refreshed versions in the submission, and repeat the comparison three times to observe the variation between trials. The order of submission does not guarantee the order of execution, and interleaving does not eliminate drift.\n"
msgstr "Patakbuhin ang parehong bersyon sa parehong QPU, na may parehong shot count at error suppression settings. I-interleave ang naiulat at na-refresh na mga bersyon sa submission, at ulitin ang paghahambing nang tatlong beses para makita ang pagkakaiba-iba sa pagitan ng mga trial. Hindi ginagarantiya ng pagkakasunod-sunod ng submission ang pagkakasunod-sunod ng execution, at hindi inaalis ng interleaving ang drift.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the output distributions {#compare-the-output-distributions}"
msgstr "Ihambing ang mga output distribution {#compare-the-output-distributions}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute the Hellinger fidelity between each measured distribution and the ideal GHZ distribution. A value of 1 means that the distributions match. This metric measures agreement only in the computational basis. It does not measure the coherence between $|0\\cdots0\\rangle$ and $|1\\cdots1\\rangle$, so it is an upper bound on the GHZ state fidelity, not a certificate of entanglement.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang Hellinger fidelity sa pagitan ng bawat nasukat na distribution at ng ideal na GHZ distribution. Ang halagang 1 ay nangangahulugang magkatugma ang mga distribution. Sinusukat lang ng metric na ito ang pagkakatugma sa computational basis. Hindi nito sinusukat ang coherence sa pagitan ng $|0\\cdots0\\rangle$ at $|1\\cdots1\\rangle$, kaya ito ay upper bound sa fidelity ng GHZ state, hindi isang katibayan ng entanglement.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The plot shows the mean across trials. The error bars indicate one standard deviation.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng plot ang mean sa lahat ng trial. Ang mga error bar ay nagpapahiwatig ng isang standard deviation.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/selection-results-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/refresh-backend-properties-with-real-time-benchmarking/extracted-outputs/selection-results-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this run, the refreshed properties changed some or all of the selected qubits at every size, and the refreshed layouts gave a higher mean fidelity for seven of the eight GHZ states. The largest gain was for the 25-qubit state, where the mean fidelity increased from 0.629 to 0.694. The refreshed layout scored higher in every trial for the 5-, 10-, 20-, 25-, 35-, and 40-qubit states. Not every size improved. For the 15-qubit state, the refreshed layout was slightly worse (0.813 compared with 0.821). For the 30-qubit state, the difference (0.596 compared with 0.591) is within the variation between trials.\n"
msgstr "Sa run na ito, binago ng mga na-refresh na property ang ilan o lahat ng napiling qubit sa bawat laki, at ang mga na-refresh na layout ay nagbigay ng mas mataas na mean fidelity para sa pito sa walong GHZ state. Ang pinakamalaking pagbuti ay sa 25-qubit na state, kung saan tumaas ang mean fidelity mula 0.629 hanggang 0.694. Mas mataas ang naging score ng na-refresh na layout sa bawat trial para sa 5-, 10-, 20-, 25-, 35-, at 40-qubit na mga state. Hindi bumuti ang bawat laki. Para sa 15-qubit na state, bahagyang mas masama ang na-refresh na layout (0.813 kumpara sa 0.821). Para sa 30-qubit na state, ang pagkakaiba (0.596 kumpara sa 0.591) ay nasa loob ng pagkakaiba-iba sa pagitan ng mga trial.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-02
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Refreshed properties do not guarantee better results. The benefit depends on how far the device has drifted since its last calibration. Also, the characterization is itself a noisy snapshot. The transpiler can select a qubit or gate that happens to measure well, even if that qubit or gate does not perform better. Shot noise, further drift between characterization and execution, and differences in characterization methodology also affect the comparison. Use the measured change and its variation to decide whether refreshed properties are useful for your workload.\n"
msgstr "Hindi ginagarantiya ng mga na-refresh na property ang mas magagandang resulta. Nakadepende ang benepisyo sa kung gaano kalayo ang naging drift ng device mula sa huling calibration nito. Gayundin, ang characterization mismo ay isang maingay na snapshot. Maaaring pumili ang transpiler ng qubit o gate na nagkataong maganda ang sukat, kahit hindi naman talaga mas maganda ang performance ng qubit o gate na iyon. Nakakaapekto rin sa paghahambing ang shot noise, karagdagang drift sa pagitan ng characterization at execution, at mga pagkakaiba sa characterization methodology. Gamitin ang nasukat na pagbabago at ang pagkakaiba-iba nito para magpasya kung kapaki-pakinabang ang mga na-refresh na property para sa iyong workload.\n"

